// expect-error: T210
// Z3 corpus #27: axis-1 — Wall 4 Step 1 refinement violation via reassignment.
//
// WHAT THIS FIXTURE PROVES
//
// Reassignment of a refined-typed binding goes through the same typed-AST
// node (`RecordConstructExpr`) as construction, so the refinement check
// fires identically. This fixture closes V5's mutation-path test gap:
// the first construction satisfies the predicate (value > 100), but the
// reassignment supplies `value: 42`, which is refutable. T210 fires on
// the reassignment site.
//
// Per V15 the refinement check has a single entry point
// (`infer_record_construct_expr`); reassignment routes through this
// entry too. The CI grep-lint asserts this single-entry invariant.
//
// THE LANGUAGE PRIMITIVES THIS NEEDED
//
// Wall 1 Step 1 already allows reassignment of non-cap aggregate types.
// Wall 4 Step 1 adds the refinement check at construction; this fixture
// proves that the reassignment lowering inherits the check without
// extra plumbing.
//
// MUTATION CONTRACT
//
// Deleting the mutation site leaves only `Index { value: 200 }`, which
// satisfies `value > 100` and compiles cleanly. The fixture would then
// be expect-ok (overlapping #25's role).
module sigil;

record Index { value: i64 } where value > 100

entry actor Main {
    on Tick() -> i64 {
        let mut idx: Index = Index { value: 200 };
        idx = Index { value: 42 };  // MUTATION_SITE
        return 1;
    }
}
